---
// The privacy policy: for the asciicharts plugin/skill (what Anthropic's directory links to) and this site.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const updated = "2026-09-27";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — asciicharts"
  description="What the asciicharts plugin, skill, command line, MCP server and website collect: nothing about you."
>
  <main class="wrap privacy">
    <p><a href="/">← asciicharts.online</a></p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p>
      asciicharts collects no personal data. It has no accounts, no analytics, no tracking and no advertising,
      and it does not sell or share anything, because it has nothing to share.
    </p>

    <h2>The plugin and skill</h2>
    <p>
      The asciicharts plugin for Claude (the skill in <code>skills/asciicharts</code>) is instructions plus a
      Python script. It runs inside your Claude session. When a chart can be rendered exactly, the skill runs
      the bundled script, <code>scripts/asciicharts.py</code>, on your machine or in your session's sandbox, or
      the <code>achart</code> command if you installed it. The script reads only the chart spec or the CSV file it
      is given, prints the chart, and exits. It makes no network requests, writes no files and keeps nothing.
    </p>
    <p>
      The numbers you chart go to Claude as part of your conversation, like anything else you type. How Anthropic
      handles your conversations is set by{" "}
      <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">Anthropic's privacy policy</a>, not by this one.
    </p>

    <h2>The command line and the MCP server</h2>
    <p>
      <code>achart</code> and <code>asciicharts-mcp</code> are programs you run yourself. They render charts from
      the input they receive and send nothing anywhere. An MCP server you deploy is operated by you; we run
      no public instance.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      asciicharts.online is a static site served by Cloudflare. It sets no cookies and loads no third-party
      scripts or fonts. Your browser's local storage keeps two display preferences, the color theme and whether
      charts are shown in color; they never leave your browser. As the host, Cloudflare processes the technical
      data every web request carries, such as your IP address, under{" "}
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Source code</h2>
    <p>
      Everything above can be checked in the open source code at{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/asciicharts">github.com/boligolov/asciicharts</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy:{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/asciicharts/issues">open an issue on GitHub</a>. If this policy
      changes, the new version is published on this page with a new date.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding-top: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .privacy h1 {
    margin: 24px 0 4px;
  }
  .privacy h2 {
    margin: 32px 0 8px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .privacy-updated {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
